<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morlaàs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morlaàs is a small town north-east of Pau in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basses-pyrenees">Pyrénées-Atlantiques</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In the 11th and 12th centuries it was the capital of the viscounts of Béarn, whose mint there struck the widely circulated Morlaàs pennies, and its church of Sainte-Foy has a notable Romanesque portal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morlaas.jpg" alt="Morlaàs" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: France64160 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mairie_de_Morla%C3%A0s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
